[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:8. The Best and the Worst]
[00:00.660]Passage 8 | 文章八
[00:02.275]The Best and the Worst | 最好与最差
[00:06.020]Joe Saunders has the most beautiful garden in our town. | 乔·桑德斯拥有我们镇上最美丽的花园。
[00:11.915]Nearly everybody enters for the nicest garden competition each year, | 几乎每个人每年都会参加最美丽花园比赛，
[00:17.855]but Joe wins every time. | 但乔每次都赢。
[00:20.955]Bill Frith's garden is larger than Joe's. | 比尔·弗里斯的花园比乔的大。
[00:25.175]Bill works harder than Joe, | 比尔比乔更努力地工作，
[00:27.265]and grows more flowers and vegetables. | 种植更多的花卉和蔬菜。
[00:30.025]But Joe's garden is more interesting. | 但乔的花园更有趣。
[00:33.270]He has made neat paths | 他修建了整洁的小径，
[00:35.705]and has built a wooden bridge over a pool. | 并在池塘上建了一座木桥。
[00:39.320]I like gardens too, | 我也喜欢花园，
[00:41.855]but I do not like hard work. | 但我不喜欢辛苦劳作。
[00:44.455]Every year I enter for the garden competition too, | 每年我也参加花园比赛，
[00:48.845]and I always win a little prize | 我总是能赢得一个小奖，
[00:51.100]for the worst garden in the town. | 颁给镇上最糟糕的花园。